@@ -0,0 +1,85 @@
+# v3.13.54 — Bank-account fatal root cause + REST hardening
+
+## Root cause of the wpcomsh HTML/CSS fatal on Payout → Bank account
+
+Every branch of the plugin that tried to send an operational alert to the
+admin — bank account change, Stripe dispute webhook, Shippo void error and
+polling timeout, seller debit posting — called
+`MNU_Ops::notify_admin( $subject, $body, $data )`.
+
+**That method was never defined on `MNU_Ops`.**
+
+The only guards were `class_exists( 'MNU_Ops' )`, which returns true (the
+class exists — it just doesn't have this particular method), so PHP proceeded
+to invoke a static method that had never been declared, producing:
+
+    Error: Call to undefined method MNU_Ops::notify_admin()
+
+On WordPress.com Atomic that fatal is rendered as the `wpcomsh-fatal` HTML/CSS
+template — the raw markup the mobile app was displaying inside the Bank
+account error card.
+
+### Fix (`includes/class-mnu-ops.php`)
+
+- Implemented `MNU_Ops::notify_admin( string $subject, string $body, array $data = [] ): void` with the shape all five callers assume.
+- Delivers via three independent channels, each wrapped in a Throwable
+  boundary so a delivery failure can never itself become a REST fatal:
+  1. `wp_mail` to `admin_email`.
+  2. Ring buffer of the last 100 alerts in the `mnu_admin_alerts` option
+     (auditable from admin UI).
+  3. Expo push to any user with `mnu_receive_admin_alerts = 1` in user meta
+     plus the admin user account itself.
+
+### Defence-in-depth at every caller
+
+Upgraded all `class_exists( 'MNU_Ops' )` guards that call `notify_admin` to
+additionally check `method_exists( 'MNU_Ops', 'notify_admin' )`:
+
+- `includes/class-mnu-bank-account.php`
+- `includes/class-mnu-native-checkout.php`
+- `includes/class-mnu-auto-label.php` (both branches — ERROR and timeout)
+- `includes/class-mnu-seller-debit.php` (previously unguarded — now wrapped)
+
+## Additional CRITICAL REST fatal surfaces closed
+
+The v3.13.53 audit surfaced eight seller-authenticated REST callbacks that
+had no Throwable boundary and would leak the wpcomsh HTML template on any
+downstream Woo, Jetpack Sync, or HPOS fatal. All eight are now wrapped:
+
+| Endpoint | File:line | Was |
+| :-- | :-- | :-- |
+| `seller_orders` | `class-tnm-rest.php:1655` | no boundary |
+| `seller_order_update` | `class-tnm-rest.php:1666` | no boundary + TypeError on `wc_get_order() === false` |
+| `seller_analytics` | `class-tnm-rest.php:1706` | no boundary; ~200-line body |
+| `seller_analytics_export` | `class-tnm-rest.php:1917` | no boundary |
+| `seller_product_create` | `class-tnm-rest.php:1344` | no boundary + `wc_get_product()` null-deref |
+| `seller_product_update` | `class-tnm-rest.php:1369` | no boundary + `wc_get_product()` null-deref |
+| `seller_product_delete` | `class-tnm-rest.php:1391` | no boundary |
+| `seller_product_duplicate` | `class-tnm-rest.php:1402` | no boundary |
+| `seller_product_variations_save` | `class-tnm-rest.php:2013` | no boundary + missing id sanity |
+
+Each wrapper follows the v3.13.53 pattern: try/catch `\Throwable`, log
+`[MyNest v3.13.54] <endpoint> failure for user %d: %s in %s:%d`, return
+`tnm_json_error( '<endpoint>_server_error', 'The website is having trouble responding. Please try again.', 500 )`.
+
+For the two long-bodied analytics methods (`seller_analytics`,
+`seller_analytics_export`) the original body was renamed to a private `*_impl`
+method and the public entry became a thin try/catch wrapper — same runtime
+behavior, contained blast radius.
+
+For `seller_order_update` an explicit `wc_get_order() instanceof WC_Order`
+null-guard was added before feeding the result to the strictly-typed
+`seller_order_to_array( WC_Order $order, int $seller_id )` — the previous
+implementation was a TypeError waiting for an invalid `id` parameter.
+
+For `seller_product_variations_save` an `absint( $request['id'] ) > 0` guard
+was added before delegating to `TNM_Marketplace::save_product_variations` —
+which downstream `wc_get_product( 0 )`s and then `->save()`s.
+
+## Expected result after deploying this plugin
+
+The Bank account save (POST `/wp-json/the-nest/v1/seller/bank-account`) will
+now either succeed cleanly or return a well-formed JSON 500 with a friendly
+message — never again the raw wpcomsh HTML that the mobile app was rendering
+verbatim. All admin alerts (bank change, disputes, void failures, debits)
+will be delivered by email + push + the audit ring.
